      "title": "Show HN: BBRouter – Ben Eater's 8-bit computer, simulated on 3D breadboards",
      "url": "https://bbrouter.com/bbrouter/ben-eater-sap-1",
      "source_feed_ids": [
        "hacker-news-frontpage"
      ],
      "published_at": "2026-11-01T00:10:30Z",
      "authors": [
        "creack"
      ],
      "categories": [],
      "guid": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50321522",
      "summary": "Hi HN, I kept wiring Ben Eater's 8-bit computer wrong, so I built a realistic virtual breadboard editor. Some of the nice features are side-by-side diff, scope, schematics auto-sync, auto-router (BBRouter stands for breadboard router), and my favorites: upload from the real Arduino IDE and connect to your AI with MCP, let Claude & co build it or help you troubleshoot. The link is the SAP-1 running. You can orbit it, probe a hole with the scope, slow the clock down, play with the virtual displays for debugging, then you can actually build it following the step-by-step instructions. A side-goal is to create a community, there are quite a lot of simulators out there but mostly offline / too abstract to realistically use it for a real build. I also never found one that had a decent UI/UX and worked well on mobile or with a trackpad. Happy to answer anything, and tell me what breaks. p.s. Maker plan is $7/month; code HACKERNEWS makes the first month free and then $5/month for as long as you keep it. Comments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50321522 Points: 4 # Comments: 0",
      "published_raw": "Sun, 01 Nov 2026 00:10:30 +0000",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-01T00:10:30Z",
      "updated_raw": "Sun, 01 Nov 2026 00:10:30 +0000",
      "language": "en"
    },
